# {{name}}

An HTTP service on [id_effect](https://github.com/Industrial/id_effect), generated by `id-effect new --template service`.

```sh
cargo test     # the router in process
{{#if pg}}
docker compose up -d db
export DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres
{{/if}}
cargo run      # http://127.0.0.1:8080/health (variables: .env.example)
```

| Route | What |
|---|---|
| `GET /` | the greeting, counted in `greetings_total` |
| `GET /health` | liveness: `200` while the process runs |
| `GET /ready` | readiness: the `HealthRegistry` checks as JSON, `503` when one is down |
| `GET /metrics` | Prometheus text: `http_server_requests_total` by method, route and status, runtime gauges |

Every request passes through `SecurityLayer::recommended`: CSRF tokens on state-changing requests, a nonce-based CSP, HSTS / `X-Frame-Options` / `nosniff` headers and signed cookies (`COOKIE_KEY`).

## Layout

- `src/lib.rs` — `app()`: the router, testable without a socket.
- `src/main.rs` — loads `HOST`, `PORT`, `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_SECS` and `COOKIE_KEY`, serves until SIGINT / SIGTERM and drains in-flight requests.
{{#if pg}}
- `src/db.rs` — the PostgreSQL pool (`DATABASE_URL`), `migrations/0001_init.sql` run on start, the `db` check behind `/ready`.
{{/if}}
- `tests/http.rs` — the routes, the security headers, readiness and metrics.

## Run it elsewhere

- `docker compose up --build` — the image from `Dockerfile` and the services it needs.
- `config/deploy.yml` — a [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org) config: set the image, servers and registry, then `kamal setup`.
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — fmt, clippy, test and a docker build on every push.

## Batteries

`Cargo.toml` enables the `id_effect_kit` features [{{kit_features}}]. `id-effect new --template service --db pg` wires the `sql-pg` feature (PostgreSQL client, migration, `db` readiness check); `--otel` the `otel` feature (OTLP export of traces, metrics and logs, configured by the `OTEL_*` variables).
